{
  "name": "Day12B: Complex Chat with Postgres memory LOCKED",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Objective\n\nBy the end of Day 12 students should understand:\n\n- Why LLMs are stateless\n- Why chat appears stateful\n- Conversation memory\n- Session IDs\n- Memory storage\n- Short-term vs Long-term memory\n- Why databases are required\n- Memory retrieval\n- Privacy considerations\n\n### Highlights\n- multiple Agents can share the same LLM.\n- The Context is owned by the agent (not the LLM), and the agent uses memory to maintain the state (conversation history)\n\n\nNote: *that this is not yet about memory or multi-agent systems—that comes later.*\n\n#[Guide](https://docs.n8n.io/workflows/components/sticky-notes/)",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 496
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1952,
        -1712
      ],
      "id": "099a95c7-ff0d-4aba-9a12-f1a3b038a313",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": "llama-3.1-8b-instant",
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.lmChatGroq",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1408,
